WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:17.374
When Sara returned from her errands, she saw Miss Minchin.

2
00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:21.718
The headmistress had just come downstairs to scold the cook.

3
00:00:21.719 --> 00:00:25.908
"Where have you been, Sara?" Miss Minchin demanded.

4
00:00:25.909 --> 00:00:29.045
"You've been out for hours!"

5
00:00:29.046 --> 00:00:33.277
"I've been doing errands for the cook," Sara answered.

6
00:00:33.278 --> 00:00:38.266
"It was hard to walk quickly because the streets are so wet and muddy."

7
00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:44.228
"Don't make excuses and don't tell lies!" Miss Minchin shouted at Sara.

8
00:00:44.229 --> 00:00:48.075
Then she went back upstairs.

9
00:00:48.076 --> 00:00:54.077
Sara went to see the cook, who was in a bad mood because of Miss Minchin's scolding.

10
00:00:54.078 --> 00:00:59.382
"You're so late!" The cook was happy to have someone to shout at.

11
00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:04.278
Sara laid her bundles on the table. "Here are your things.

12
00:01:04.279 --> 00:01:08.703
May I have something to eat?" she asked softly.

13
00:01:08.704 --> 00:01:14.966
"Supper is finished!" the cook snapped. "There's some bread in the pantry.

14
00:01:14.967 --> 00:01:19.253
That's all you'll get this time of day."

15
00:01:19.254 --> 00:01:25.918
Sara found the bread. It was old and hard and dry, but she ate it anyway.

16
00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:29.557
Then she climbed slowly upstairs to her room.

17
00:01:29.558 --> 00:01:33.546
She was glad to see a glimmer of light under her door.

18
00:01:33.547 --> 00:01:38.865
That meant Ermengarde had come to visit. She pushed open the door.

19
00:01:38.866 --> 00:01:43.516
Ermengarde sat in the middle of the bed, with her feet tucked under her.

20
00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:47.139
She had her red shawl wrapped around her shoulders.

21
00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:51.768
"I didn't expect to see you tonight, Ermengarde," Sara said.

22
00:01:51.769 --> 00:01:57.762
"Miss Amelia has gone out to visit an old aunt," Ermengarde explained.

23
00:01:57.763 --> 00:02:02.358
"No one else ever comes and looks into the bedrooms after we're in bed.

24
00:02:02.359 --> 00:02:06.598
I could stay here until morning if I wanted to."

25
00:02:06.599 --> 00:02:10.419
Ermengarde pointed to the table under the skylight.

26
00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:15.010
"Oh, Sara!" said Ermengarde in despair.

27
00:02:15.011 --> 00:02:19.871
"Look what my father sent me. More books!"

28
00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:26.729
Sara's mood brightened instantly. "Oh, these are beautiful books!

29
00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:32.063
I've always wanted to read this one about the French Revolution."

30
00:02:32.064 --> 00:02:38.413
"Well, I don't want to read it. I know he'll test me on all of these books.

31
00:02:38.414 --> 00:02:43.092
But I still don't want to read any of them."

32
00:02:43.093 --> 00:02:49.939
"Do you know what we could do?" Sara said eagerly. Her cheeks were flushed.

33
00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:54.278
"I could read the books, and then I could describe them to you.

34
00:02:54.279 --> 00:02:57.693
It would be like telling you stories!"

35
00:02:57.694 --> 00:03:01.920
"That's a wonderful idea!" said Ermengarde.

36
00:03:01.921 --> 00:03:06.519
"I've been doing better since you helped me with my French lessons."

37
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.714
"I've been helping Lottie with her math too," Sara said.

38
00:03:10.715 --> 00:03:17.416
"Miss Minchin has no idea why we're suddenly so smart!" Ermengarde said.

39
00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:19.732
The two girls laughed.

40
00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:24.293
Sara suddenly started and looked up at the skylight.

41
00:03:24.294 --> 00:03:27.334
"Did you hear something?" she asked.

42
00:03:27.335 --> 00:03:30.547
"No," said Ermengarde.

43
00:03:30.548 --> 00:03:38.693
"It sounded like somebody was dragging something across the roof," Sara said. "Maybe it was—"

44
00:03:38.694 --> 00:03:41.718
This time they both heard the same sound.

45
00:03:41.719 --> 00:03:44.389
But it wasn't coming from the roof.

46
00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:48.562
It was Miss Minchin's voice, and she sounded angry.

47
00:03:48.563 --> 00:03:51.473
Sara quickly put out the candle.

48
00:03:51.474 --> 00:04:00.435
"Miss Minchin is scolding Becky," whispered Sara. "She's making Becky cry."

49
00:04:00.436 --> 00:04:05.266
"Will Miss Minchin come in here?" Ermengarde was in a panic.

50
00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:11.243
"No, she'll think I'm asleep. Stay still!" Sara whispered.

51
00:04:11.244 --> 00:04:15.763
It was very rare for Miss Minchin to come up the stairs to the attic.

52
00:04:15.764 --> 00:04:19.951
Sara could only think of one other time that she'd done so.

53
00:04:19.952 --> 00:04:24.479
But now she was angry enough to be coming at least part of the way up.

54
00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.632
"You rude, lying child!" Miss Minchin shouted at Becky.

55
00:04:29.633 --> 00:04:34.570
"The cook tells me things are constantly being stolen from the kitchen."

56
00:04:34.571 --> 00:04:39.294
"It isn't me!" Becky began to sob.

57
00:04:39.295 --> 00:04:44.684
"I'm hungry all the time, but I don't steal food!"

58
00:04:44.685 --> 00:04:47.405
Miss Minchin sounded out of breath.

59
00:04:47.406 --> 00:04:52.500
"You should go to prison for stealing that piece of meat pie!"

60
00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:56.099
She slapped Becky. "Go to bed!"

61
00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:00.026
"It wasn't me!" Becky insisted.

62
00:05:00.027 --> 00:05:04.393
And again Sara and Ermengarde heard the sound of a slap.

63
00:05:04.394 --> 00:05:07.581
Miss Minchin stomped down the stairs.

64
00:05:07.582 --> 00:05:11.833
Sara and Ermengarde heard Becky crying in the next room.

65
00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:16.491
"I didn't take it!" Becky sobbed.

66
00:05:16.492 --> 00:05:21.637
"The cook gave it to her boyfriend, the policeman!"

67
00:05:21.638 --> 00:05:25.556
"This makes me so angry!" Sara said.

68
00:05:25.557 --> 00:05:30.784
She stood in the center of the dark room, clenching her fists furiously.

69
00:05:30.785 --> 00:05:37.317
"The cook is wicked and cruel. She's the one who's stealing, not Becky!"

70
00:05:37.318 --> 00:05:40.084
Sara lit her candle again.

71
00:05:40.085 --> 00:05:45.866
"Poor Becky is always hungry. Sometimes she eats crusts out of the trash!"

72
00:05:45.867 --> 00:05:52.037
To Ermengarde's surprise Sara burst into tears.

73
00:05:52.038 --> 00:05:56.074
"Oh, Sara." Ermengarde looked at Sara.

74
00:05:56.075 --> 00:06:00.645
For the first time, she noticed how thin her friend was.

75
00:06:00.646 --> 00:06:05.096
"I hate to ask this, but are you ever hungry?"

76
00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:10.521
"Yes!" Sara burst out. "I'm hungry all the time.

77
00:06:10.522 --> 00:06:14.571
I'm so hungry right now that I could almost eat you!

78
00:06:14.572 --> 00:06:18.641
And Becky is even hungrier than I am."

79
00:06:18.642 --> 00:06:28.524
"Oh, I had no idea!" said Ermengarde. "But I know just what to do."
